=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
A thorough end-to-end investigation of the reported symptom — PC5 (172.16.10.5,
VLAN 10) unable to reach the design group (172.16.30.x, VLAN 30) — found no
fault in the network.

The inter-VLAN routing path works as follows: PC5 sends traffic to its default
gateway 172.16.10.254, which is the VLAN 10 SVI on mswitch0 (the distribution-
layer multilayer switch). mswitch0 has IP forwarding enabled and hosts three
active SVIs: vlan10 (172.16.10.254/24), vlan20 (172.16.20.254/24), and vlan30
(172.16.30.254/24). A directly-connected route for 172.16.30.0/24 via the vlan30
interface is present in mswitch0's routing table. Downstream, switch3 correctly
bridges VLAN 30 access ports (eth2–eth5, serving PC12–PC14) to mswitch0 via the
eth0.30 sub-interface. There are no iptables rules on mswitch0 that block
forwarded traffic.

Live ping tests from PC5 to all three VLAN 30 hosts — 172.16.30.12 (pc12),
172.16.30.13 (pc13), and 172.16.30.14 (pc14) — completed with 0% packet loss
and TTL=63, confirming correct single-hop L3 forwarding through mswitch0 in both
directions. All VLAN 30 hosts have their default gateway set to 172.16.30.254,
ensuring return traffic is routed correctly.

Root cause: There is no fault. The described symptom does not exist in the
current lab state; PC5 can reach all 172.16.30.x design-group machines without
any packet loss. No corrective action is required.
=== END ===
